From 017107e070940c02b9fffe5d9421cbbd0b5b2f87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: isoriano1968 <81116077+isoriano1968@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 06:24:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] NNNNN usbvc: camera terminal controls (exposure, focus), more
 processing unit controls, V4L2_CTRL_FLAG_NEXT_CTRL

Only brightness, contrast, saturation, hue and gamma were offered, and
only by probing their IDs one by one.  Programs that list controls with
V4L2_CTRL_FLAG_NEXT_CTRL (GStreamer's extra-controls) found none, and the
camera terminal had no controls at all: a C920 with auto exposure
priority on halves its frame rate in low light, and it could not be
turned off.

- usbvc: control table with the V4L2 control ID, unit (processing unit
  or camera terminal), selector, length, bmControls bit and type, sorted
  by ID; Linux's control names.
- usbvc: new controls: white balance automatic and temperature, gain,
  power line frequency (menu), sharpness, backlight compensation; auto
  exposure (menu: auto, manual, shutter and aperture priority, from
  CT_AE_MODE's bitmap), exposure time absolute, exposure dynamic
  framerate (CT_AE_PRIORITY), focus absolute and automatic continuous.
- usbvc: VIDIOC_QUERYCTRL with V4L2_CTRL_FLAG_NEXT_CTRL; VIDIOC_QUERYMENU.
- usbvc: values of 1, 2 or 4 bytes; brightness and hue are signed.
- usbvc: bmControls bits 8 and above were tested at the wrong bit.
